WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.427
The first project step is inspection.

00:00:02.427 --> 00:00:06.342
In Spark, printSchema helps you see column types.

00:00:06.342 --> 00:00:12.462
show displays sample records. count can be useful, but remember that it triggers work.

00:00:12.462 --> 00:00:14.207
Use it intentionally.

00:00:14.207 --> 00:00:20.542
Before writing transformations, know what the raw data looks like and what one row represents.

00:00:20.542 --> 00:00:26.207
Connect this idea to a lakehouse processing millions of web events across many files.

00:00:26.207 --> 00:00:31.767
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:39.452
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:39.452 --> 00:00:44.682
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:44.682 --> 00:00:50.309
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
